   "text": "Share of users who left before reaching a doctor, control (grey) vs treatment (orange), by department."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 2074,
   "x": 280,
   "w": 880,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "In dermatology, 12.7% of treatment users gave up before reaching a doctor, against 7.7% in control, and completion fell from 85.0% to 80.5%. Dermatology is the only department where treatment completed less often than control."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 2196,
   "x": 280,
   "w": 880,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The difference is not noise. Its z-score is 4.65, compared with 1.72 for the overall loss gap. It also shows up in every dermatology complaint and in each of the 6 weeks of the test: weekly treatment loss ranged from 11.0% to 15.9%, while control ranged from 6.3% to 8.7%."
  },
  {
